---
description: Content architecture — site data, Sanity GROQ
globs: lib/**/*.js,content/**/*,scripts/**/*.js
---

- `lib/data.js` is the single source of truth for site-wide structured
  content (nav, sponsors, directors, chapters, advisors, contact info,
  recommendation letters). Add new structured content there rather than
  hardcoding it in page files — see `nextjs-app-router.mdc`.
- Posts, events, stories, and galleries are edited in Sanity Studio
  (`mllws-sanity`). This site reads **published** documents via GROQ in
  `lib/cms.js` (`force-static` + `revalidateTag`). Never query drafts on
  the public site. Never query Neon.
- Access goes through `lib/posts.js`, `lib/events.js`, `lib/stories.js`,
  and `lib/galleries.js`. Pages should import from there, not create a
  Sanity client.
- If `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID` is unset or a query fails, return
  empty lists — never crash `npm run dev` or `npm run build`.
- Drafts stay in Sanity. Do not commit unpublished content into this
  public repo. Leftover `/content/cms/` and `/content/blog/` stay
  gitignored.
